#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100593 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101007 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e3833c1-4ec5-5681-ae69-6a9cceece871" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Slope and Y-Intercept From the Equation of a Line"}] :question/id #uuid "95fc8e7d-776c-5d09-9140-a83dc575ac79" :question/math-academy-id "e-12851" :question/problem "What are the slope and $y$-intercept of the line $y=2x-9?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation is in slope-intercept form $y={\\color{red}{m}}x+{\\color{blue}{b}},$ where $\\color{red}{m}$ is the slope and $\\color{blue}{b}$ is the $y$-intercept.\n\nFor the equation $y=2x-9,$ we see that the slope is ${\\color{red}{m=2}}$ and the $y$-intercept is ${\\color{blue}{b=-9}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100594 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8e10b2d-cad1-5d50-b9fc-917c3367f814" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Graphed Line (Positive Slope)"}] :question/id #uuid "36e13cef-f61a-53e2-8f0e-9ff567dc6fb6" :question/math-academy-id "e-12852" :question/problem "![](images/46/46a04d55edd836050d30a0d4d52c4c441619babd79f93f3540f61a5f437a1ea7.png)\n\nThe line shown above passes through the points $(0,-2)$ and $(2,2).$" :question/worked-solution "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b.$ So, we need to work out the slope $m$ and the $y$-intercept $b.$\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the line intercepts the $y$-axis at $(0,-2).$ So, the $y$-intercept is $b = -2.$\n\nWe can calculate the slope of the line by choosing two points on the line and applying the slope formula. The line passes through the points $(0,-2)$ and $(2,2),$ so we calculate its slope as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-(-2)}{2-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the slope $m = 2$ and the $y$-intercept $b = -2$ into the slope-intercept form $y = mx + b,$ we obtain the equation of the line:\n\n$$\ny = 2x - 2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100595 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4762cb71-f6b6-5d32-8d0b-a457db66ff97" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Line That Passes Through Two Points: Y-Intercept Given"}] :question/id #uuid "8351e1cb-c602-5968-be5a-9c337ad977de" :question/math-academy-id "e-12853" :question/problem "Calculate the equation of the straight line that passes through the points $(0,8)$ and $(3,2).$" :question/worked-solution "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b.$ So, we need to work out the slope $m$ and the $y$-intercept $b.$\n\nFirst, we calculate the slope $m$ using the given points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-8}{3-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6}{3} \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coordinates of the $y$-intercept are always $(0,{\\color{blue}{b}}).$ We know that the line passes through the point $(0,{\\color{blue}{8}}),$ so the $y$-intercept is $b={\\color{blue}{8}}.$ \n\nSubstituting the slope $m=-2$ and the $y$-intercept $b=8$ into the slope-intercept formula $y=mx+b,$ we reach\n\n$$\ny=-2x+8.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100617 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101009 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ac060cb-0c76-5050-9156-e5f17ad26fbb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Graphed Line (Negative Slope)"}] :question/id #uuid "206b8f86-4184-50fa-9999-08700d10dc4f" :question/math-academy-id "e-20867" :question/problem "Find the equation of the line shown below.\n\n![](images/42/4298ec9c12555fd5e87265617ee274ef0fa859decd3ccd9473dfe8f778492df0.png)" :question/worked-solution "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b.$ So, we need to work out the slope $m$ and the $y$-intercept $b.$\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the line intercepts the $y$-axis at $(0,2).$ So, the $y$-intercept is $b=2.$\n\nWe can calculate the slope of the line by choosing two points on the line and applying the slope formula. The line passes through the points $(0,2)$ and $(6,0),$ so we calculate its slope as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-2}{6-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{6} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the slope $m=-\\dfrac{1}{3}$ and the $y$-intercept $b=2$ into the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b,$ we obtain the equation of the line:\n\n$$\ny=-\\dfrac{1}{3}x+2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101240 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101007 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e3833c1-4ec5-5681-ae69-6a9cceece871" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Slope and Y-Intercept From the Equation of a Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f1f9105-48d3-52a5-8a6b-793e8c21210e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490728}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f1f9105-48d3-52a5-8a6b-793e8c21210e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490728} :answer-field/id #uuid "64a16bc0-7e89-536a-a2fd-0afc037a1fba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098775} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e27c10e5-5697-5e66-9c52-1802c0c760e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e27c10e5-5697-5e66-9c52-1802c0c760e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490941} :answer-field/id #uuid "78cde657-671c-56b7-936f-dbc0cf54fa26" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098776}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7a568a73-edca-58dd-acc8-ad4fc1b68903" :question/math-academy-id "q-171689" :question/problem "Determine the slope and $y$-intercept of the line $y=4x-3.$\n\nThe slope of the line is\n{{field-1}}\n and the $y$-intercept is\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The equation is in slope-intercept form $y=mx+b,$ where $m$ is the slope and $b$ is the $y$-intercept.\n\nFor the equation $y=4x-3,$ we see that the slope is $m=4$ and the $y$-intercept is $b=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491180 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101009 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ac060cb-0c76-5050-9156-e5f17ad26fbb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Graphed Line (Negative Slope)"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e0afc9d-f9e4-5c4c-9189-e3cdc71ed705" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e0afc9d-f9e4-5c4c-9189-e3cdc71ed705" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490725} :answer-field/id #uuid "2935d3f9-03e7-5bb2-8b88-1d26fc3e9e62" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491021} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f0d1e1a-e15c-501c-9015-e2e2abd1094b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490630}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f0d1e1a-e15c-501c-9015-e2e2abd1094b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490630} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa9c5cdb-7aeb-5609-a9ff-405bf86bac38" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491069}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9c04f73c-b1f7-5a12-9163-6dcdb2ddf789" :question/math-academy-id "q-171701" :question/problem "![](images/8d/8d59cf7d27ed6e7912a53e6ef52a2193f372c15fca3d50272d3c697451ff2db5.png)\n\nGiven that the slope of the line shown above is $-3,$ the equation of the line is $y=${{field-1}}\n$x\\,-$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b.$ We know that the slope is $m=-3,$ so we just need to work out $y$-intercept $b.$\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the line intercepts the $y$-axis at $(0,-2).$ So, the $y$-intercept is $b=-2.$\n\nSubstituting the slope $m=-3$ and the $y$-intercept $b=-2$ into the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b,$ we obtain the equation of the line:\n\n$$\ny=-3x-2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491168 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4762cb71-f6b6-5d32-8d0b-a457db66ff97" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Line That Passes Through Two Points: Y-Intercept Given"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "008ca9c2-dcd7-59c9-841c-96dc71906e33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "008ca9c2-dcd7-59c9-841c-96dc71906e33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490513} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0a06e9b-07dc-516a-ad6a-3fe116353c38" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491084}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7de4ef78-0bc0-5a93-a3dc-392320077ab4" :question/math-academy-id "q-175564" :question/problem "Written in the form $y=mx+b,$ what is the equation of the line that passes through the points $(0,0)$ and $(2,4)?$\n\nThe equation of the line is $y=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b.$ So, we need to work out the slope $m$ and the $y$-intercept $b.$\n\nFirst, we calculate the slope $m$ using the given points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-0}{2-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coordinates of the $y$-intercept are always $(0,b).$ We know that the line passes through the point $(0,0),$ so the $y$-intercept is $b=0.$\n\nSubstituting the slope $m=2$ and the $y$-intercept $b=0$ into the slope-intercept formula $y=mx+b,$ we reach\n\n$$\ny=2x+0=2\\,x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101260 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4762cb71-f6b6-5d32-8d0b-a457db66ff97" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Line That Passes Through Two Points: Y-Intercept Given"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ee700eb-d3de-5139-9f6a-e06a58f49760" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ee700eb-d3de-5139-9f6a-e06a58f49760" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490662} :answer-field/id #uuid "e531a471-fcee-5258-89f1-728bfe52aaca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098886}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c0b425fb-b8a2-5723-acb7-016f2e613ac7" :question/math-academy-id "q-179507" :question/problem "Written in the form $y=mx+b,$ what is the equation of the line that passes through the points $(3,-10)$ and $(0,-4)?$\n\nThe equation of the line is $y=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b.$ So, we need to work out the slope $m$ and the $y$-intercept $b.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate the slope $m$ using the given points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4-(-10)}{0-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4+10}{0-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{-3} \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coordinates of the $y$-intercept are always $(0,b).$ We know that the line passes through the point $(0,-4),$ so the $y$-intercept is $b=-4.$\n\nSubstituting the slope $m=-2$ and the $y$-intercept $b=-4$ into the slope-intercept formula $y=mx+b,$ we reach\n\n$$\ny=-2x-4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491162 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4762cb71-f6b6-5d32-8d0b-a457db66ff97" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Line That Passes Through Two Points: Y-Intercept Given"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b3a6a57-231a-57d2-a255-fbe592970476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b3a6a57-231a-57d2-a255-fbe592970476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490717} :answer-field/id #uuid "05486e1a-5b6d-541c-8967-f8994e8b4320" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7322bdb5-3fd0-5378-80df-fffaea4252d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-179510" :question/problem "Written in the form $y=mx+b,$ what is the equation of the line that passes through the points  $(0,0)$ and $(2,-1)?$\n\nThe equation of the line is $y=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b.$ So, we need to work out the slope $m$ and the $y$-intercept $b.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate the slope $m$ using the given points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1-0}{2-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coordinates of the $y$-intercept are always $(0,b).$ We know that the line passes through the point $(0,0),$ so the $y$-intercept is $b=0.$\n\nSubstituting the slope $m=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and the $y$-intercept $b=0$ into the slope-intercept formula $y=mx+b,$ we reach\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x+0=-\\frac{1}{2}x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491158 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8e10b2d-cad1-5d50-b9fc-917c3367f814" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Graphed Line (Positive Slope)"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02fae4b4-e8cf-5758-be71-6c13e5c5c515" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490516} {:answer/id #uuid "27b3818f-6d62-5f79-b799-161420b4f7d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490582} {:answer/id #uuid "484cbc24-cece-533c-9d54-b6fae769d514" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490647} {:answer/id #uuid "7d0c30db-1ddb-5370-85db-06889107c744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{3}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490758} {:answer/id #uuid "c12dbffc-8810-53fc-a6d4-8d3bcb6adf1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27b3818f-6d62-5f79-b799-161420b4f7d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490582} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5d76f0b-3896-59e7-ada0-814f4f3910e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491074}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6c227a24-fcf2-56a8-8952-2c61a7a9ba4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-22608" :question/problem "![](images/a2/a23ec0bd4759cb8fd799954f17df8f9006ee592fbf1f59645b7693e4d9d64f17.png)\n\nThe line shown above passes through the points $(0,-1)$ and $(1,2).$ What is the equation of the line?" :question/worked-solution "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b.$ So we need to work out the slope $m$ and the $y$-intercept $b.$\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the line intercepts the $y$-axis at $(0,-1).$ So, the $y$-intercept is $b=-1.$\n\nWe can calculate the slope of the line by choosing two points on the line and applying the slope formula. The line passes through the points $(0,-1)$ and $(1,2),$ so we calculate its slope as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-(-1)}{1-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the slope $m=3$ and the $y$-intercept $b=-1$ into the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b,$ we obtain the equation of the line:\n\n$$\ny=3x-1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491145 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8e10b2d-cad1-5d50-b9fc-917c3367f814" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Graphed Line (Positive Slope)"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d38f694-da2e-5bf6-b995-92ea1d0bb10c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{3}{2}x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490533} {:answer/id #uuid "3ff220e2-4b47-5a44-94ac-9fd5bbc57fa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{3}{2}x+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490632} {:answer/id #uuid "563b6890-e658-5ec8-b9af-0b87df97c1c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{4}{3}x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490674} {:answer/id #uuid "d3eaa7a3-d7bd-5799-8737-e68639780140" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{3}{4}x+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490909} {:answer/id #uuid "f5707be3-00ae-57f3-9dc5-624a663eba65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{3}{4}x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490982}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5707be3-00ae-57f3-9dc5-624a663eba65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{3}{4}x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490982} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8280e8d-7370-5419-8f80-9e5e211764bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491089}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4f5e6228-affa-52ca-ad4e-cd380e1cf95b" :question/math-academy-id "q-22614" :question/problem "![](images/14/14b7f1e0ab3336feee7503ce45b289789a0a9ffc5e2ffbb035c71e8967a30048.png)\n\nThe line shown above passes through the points $(0,-2)$ and $(4,1).$ What is the equation of the line?" :question/worked-solution "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b.$ So, we need to work out the slope $m$ and the $y$-intercept $b.$\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the line intercepts the $y$-axis at $(0,-2).$ So, the $y$-intercept is $b=-2.$\n\nWe can calculate the slope of the line by choosing two points on the line and applying the slope formula. The line passes through the points $(0,-2)$ and $(4,1),$ so we calculate its slope as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-(-2)}{4-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the slope $m=\\frac{3}{4}$ and the $y$-intercept $b=-2$ into the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b,$ we obtain the equation of the line:\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{3}{4}x-2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491119 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101009 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ac060cb-0c76-5050-9156-e5f17ad26fbb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Graphed Line (Negative Slope)"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1132aeba-447a-5484-8f9e-8a69432727c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{4}{5}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490547} {:answer/id #uuid "7f2be597-854f-5eba-9b4a-9b6dfa58aef8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-4x+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490765} {:answer/id #uuid "8e020c59-f1bc-53b2-b36d-56e3bb5d1e0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{5}{4}x+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490794} {:answer/id #uuid "9c15e11d-aac6-5aa7-9602-3a833ec17436" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{4}{5}x+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490833} {:answer/id #uuid "eeb8bbce-ec61-5b6f-a3a1-47e0d6917e4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{4}{5}x+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eeb8bbce-ec61-5b6f-a3a1-47e0d6917e4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{4}{5}x+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490968} :answer-field/id #uuid "7479d82e-5a0d-5a83-8e2b-a0acea16c02c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491048}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "13372aad-9f96-5db2-8926-3d8b0436e154" :question/math-academy-id "q-316671" :question/problem "![](images/fe/fe1b1b8f9837ec2fbd6a7eab48b7f4575dd0e247b6d633ec5e440b43f5efc04f.png)\n\nThe line shown above passes through the points $(0,6)$ and $(5,2).$ What is the equation of the line?" :question/worked-solution "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b.$ So we need to work out the slope $m$ and the $y$-intercept $b.$\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the line intercepts the $y$-axis at $(0,6).$ So, the $y$-intercept is $b=6.$\n\nWe can calculate the slope of the line by choosing two points on the line and applying the slope formula. The line passes through the points $(0,6)$ and $(5,2),$ so we calculate its slope as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-6}{5-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4}{5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the slope $m=-\\frac{4}{5}$ and the $y$-intercept $b=6$ into the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b,$ we obtain the equation of the line:\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{4}{5}x+6\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8e10b2d-cad1-5d50-b9fc-917c3367f814" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Graphed Line (Positive Slope)"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "148d50c5-0dc3-5f7a-bce8-d6a5580bf805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490551} {:answer/id #uuid "23e24a86-5312-5906-8281-44f44127b57d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490577} {:answer/id #uuid "409ca9d8-c1aa-537f-a31a-aeac14b790e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490634} {:answer/id #uuid "6a4cdcb3-ac3f-55b1-be2c-56a1e6645cae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490714} {:answer/id #uuid "ad6e941c-849d-5e92-912b-ffb4e060ab4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad6e941c-849d-5e92-912b-ffb4e060ab4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490855} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8abdc2e-654c-5de2-a6d7-f81cec3d235d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9d57e773-1683-50b7-a75b-43650486b617" :question/math-academy-id "q-44186" :question/problem "![](images/83/832d829821a9c18af98f5c474349b09f481c225ec5b6771e0482402d44b10e38.png)\n\nGiven that the slope of the line shown above is $3,$ what is the equation of the line?" :question/worked-solution "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b.$ We know that the slope is $m=3,$ so we just need to work out $y$-intercept $b.$\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the line intercepts the $y$-axis at $(0,0).$ So, the $y$-intercept is $b=0.$\n\nSubstituting the slope $m=3$ and the $y$-intercept $b=0$ into the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b,$ we obtain the equation of the line:\n\n$$\ny=3x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491177 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8e10b2d-cad1-5d50-b9fc-917c3367f814" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Graphed Line (Positive Slope)"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a8dd128-e29f-5f7a-b146-b9a220f5e14f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490619} {:answer/id #uuid "3b7468f0-3052-50f1-9685-8716b5dcbb6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490620} {:answer/id #uuid "58b8517e-abd3-5e36-a214-2c89774f60f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}x+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490678} {:answer/id #uuid "5de0281f-42b8-5005-8f2e-765e65147ab5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490686} {:answer/id #uuid "f199dfbd-9f10-54a1-a21b-af4b8b1de9ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}x-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a8dd128-e29f-5f7a-b146-b9a220f5e14f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490619} :answer-field/id #uuid "103e53e2-1064-528c-b885-e2e5926f20a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491008}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "939195cc-3480-5b14-b0df-127e5e8e5d9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-44286" :question/problem "![](images/dd/ddb73fe5746933a3a08acc3fe2a370fbe91a944b22f5b94be1425907f83c0fed.png)\n\nDetermine the equation of the line shown above if its slope is $\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b.$ We know that the slope is $m=\\frac{1}{2},$ so we just need to work out $y$-intercept $b.$\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the line passes through the point $(2,4).$ Substituting this into $y=mx+b$ with $m=\\frac{1}{2}$ and solving for $b,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{2}x+b \\\\ 4 & =\\frac{1}{2}(2)+b \\\\ 4 & =1+b \\\\ b & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is $y=\\frac{1}{2}x+3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491202 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101007 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e3833c1-4ec5-5681-ae69-6a9cceece871" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Slope and Y-Intercept From the Equation of a Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d94c17a-20d9-55e1-9acb-fa976027e3af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The slope is $2$ and the $y$-intercept is $3.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490600} {:answer/id #uuid "402f7c00-2b87-5fe0-9e1e-233aa5e82415" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The slope is $-2$ and the $y$-intercept is $3.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490633} {:answer/id #uuid "6219c8e0-d04f-53d6-946a-8f5aeec3a9bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The slope is $3$ and the $y$-intercept is $2.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490695} {:answer/id #uuid "758b04f2-e5c1-5f8a-aeae-904c59c85f42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The slope is $-2$ and the $y$-intercept is $-3.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490743} {:answer/id #uuid "bfb6f35b-2e3b-5ebc-bde2-fce9036dbd3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The slope is $3$ and the $y$-intercept is $-2.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "402f7c00-2b87-5fe0-9e1e-233aa5e82415" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The slope is $-2$ and the $y$-intercept is $3.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490633} :answer-field/id #uuid "352af8ef-2eed-5ecf-b294-c94d703f77d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491026}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dd155880-954d-5531-a956-9c38dd5d225e" :question/math-academy-id "q-59650" :question/problem "What are the slope and $y$-intercept of the line $y=-2x+3?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation is in slope-intercept form $y=mx+b,$ where $m$ is the slope and $b$ is the $y$-intercept.\n\nFor the equation $y=-2x+3,$ we see that the slope is $m=-2$ and the $y$-intercept is $b=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491207 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4762cb71-f6b6-5d32-8d0b-a457db66ff97" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Line That Passes Through Two Points: Y-Intercept Given"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e045835-a166-5b0d-835d-5cabb6ececbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2x+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490537} {:answer/id #uuid "34909aa8-cc44-5810-a830-f56ee0fd1048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490611} {:answer/id #uuid "45177f38-cbc9-5587-89ad-4e670443ed7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2x+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490642} {:answer/id #uuid "c672c777-31ab-517e-9696-8cf1083e0f08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-4x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490892} {:answer/id #uuid "d730f643-b632-5af1-bdff-5bdd27447bda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-4x+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e045835-a166-5b0d-835d-5cabb6ececbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2x+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490537} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ef69642-bcf0-5860-9c5a-224aacb3b1f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491057}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e727ac27-525d-538d-9196-20a878c07523" :question/math-academy-id "q-6950" :question/problem "Find the equation of the line that passes through the points $(4,1)$ and $(0,9).$" :question/worked-solution "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form $y=mx+b.$ So, we need to work out the slope $m$ and the $y$-intercept $b.$\n\nFirst, we calculate the slope $m$ using the given points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-1}{0-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{-4} \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coordinates of the $y$-intercept are always $(0,b).$ We know that the line passes through the point $(0,9),$ so the $y$-intercept is $b=9.$\n\nSubstituting the slope $m=-2$ and the $y$-intercept $b=9$ into the slope-intercept formula $y=mx+b,$ we reach\n\n$$\ny=-2x+9.\n$$"}]}
